{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And you shall bring an offering, etc., to HaShem, bulls, etc.</b> It appears that the reason for the diminishing of the bulls day by day is because there are two mysteries of sevenths: the nations are the seventy nations, and they are likened to bulls; and Israel too are in the aspect of the seven, in the mystery of the Daughter of Seven (Zohar Chadash 3:262), and all their deeds are in sevenths — the offerings in all the additional sacrifices, seven and seven; the festivals, seven and seven; the Sabbath is the mystery of the seven branches of the Tree from which the root of their souls is seven; the righteous, seven. And HaShem hinted that corresponding to the nations, who are alluded to by the bulls, they would continually diminish and decrease." "<b>And He hinted</b> in this reckoning there are fixed fourteen lambs, to allude to two tiers within Israel that come by way of the allusion of the lambs — one hidden and one revealed. The hidden ones are the sparks that need to be refined from the nations, and the revealed ones are the refiners. Therefore, when the bulls are finished, this is a sign for you that the hidden has been consumed from among them, and none will remain except Israel, for a marvel and a sign. And this is what HaShem hinted in the offering of the day of assembly (Shemini Atzeret): seven lambs, for they — Israel — are the flock of holy ones; one bull is what remains of the nations from the branch of Yishmael; one ram is what remains of the descendants of Esav, who come from Yitzchak. And understand the mystery of the matter."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:15:52.851872604Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}